  faqSecDapps: 'dApps',
  faqQ1: 'How do I create a wallet?',
  faqA1: 'On the welcome screen, tap “Create a wallet”. Nova generates a 12-word recovery phrase that you must write down on paper, then you verify a few words and choose a PIN code. Your keys are created directly on your phone.',
  faqQ2: 'How do I restore a wallet?',
  faqA2: 'On the welcome screen, tap “I already have a phrase”, paste your BIP-39 recovery phrase (12 or 24 words) and choose a PIN. Your wallet and its accounts are re-derived locally.',
  faqQ3: 'Where is my secret phrase stored?',
  faqA3: 'Only on your phone, encrypted with AES-256-GCM under your PIN, in the hardware secure storage (Keystore/Keychain). It is NEVER sent over the network or stored on a server.',
  faqQ4: 'Can I change my PIN?',
  faqA4: 'Yes: Settings → Change PIN. The change re-encrypts all your vaults with the new code.',
  faqQ5: 'What if I lose my phone?',
  faqA5: 'Your funds are on the blockchain, not in the phone. Install Nova on a new device and restore with your recovery phrase. Without that phrase, no one (including you) can access the funds — hence the importance of keeping it safe.',
  faqQ6: 'Can Nova see my seed phrase?',
  faqA6: 'No. Nova is non-custodial: your phrase is encrypted on your device, decrypted on the fly only to sign, then forgotten. It never passes through our servers.',
  faqQ7: 'Why do I have to sign some transactions?',
  faqA7: 'Any action that moves funds or authorizes a contract to spend them must be signed by your private key, protected by your PIN. This is what prevents a site from doing anything without your explicit consent.',
  faqQ8: 'How do I recognize a scam?',
  faqA8: 'No legitimate party will ever ask for your recovery phrase. Beware of sites imitating a known brand (Nova warns you in red), “unlimited” approvals, and messages too good to be true. Nova also shows a security analysis (GoPlus) before each signature.',
  faqQ9: 'Why is my transaction pending?',
  faqA9: 'It is waiting to be included in a block. Network fees that are too low or heavy congestion slow it down. Nova notifies you as soon as it is confirmed.',
  faqQ10: 'How do I cancel a transaction?',
  faqA10: 'A confirmed transaction is irreversible. A still-pending transaction can sometimes be replaced (same nonce, higher fees) — this feature is not yet automated in Nova.',
  faqQ11: 'What are gas fees?',
  faqA11: 'It’s the cost paid to the network validators to process your transaction, settled in the native crypto (ETH, BNB, POL…). It varies with network congestion.',
  faqQ12: 'Why did my transaction fail?',
  faqA12: 'Common causes: insufficient balance (including fees), slippage exceeded on a swap, gas limit too low, or the contract rejected the operation. Note: the gas fees of a failed transaction are still charged.',
  faqQ13: 'How do I connect a dApp?',
  faqA13: 'Two ways: the built-in browser (Menu → dApp browser), or WalletConnect (paste the “wc:…” link). In both cases, you confirm the connection with your PIN.',
  faqQ14: 'How do I disconnect a dApp?',
  faqA14: 'WalletConnect tab: “Disconnect” for a WalletConnect session, “Forget” for a built-in browser site.',
  faqQ15: 'What is WalletConnect?',
  faqA15: 'A standard protocol that links your wallet to a dApp via a QR code or a link, without a browser extension.',
  faqQ16: 'How do I revoke an approval?',
  faqA16: 'Menu → Approvals: Nova lists the contracts you have allowed to spend your tokens. Revoke those you no longer use (it’s a transaction, with network fees).',
  faqQ17: 'How do I switch networks?',
  faqA17: 'From the home screen (the network badge) or Settings → Network. The same address works on all EVM networks; only the queried network changes.',
  faqQ18: 'How do I add an RPC network?',
  faqA18: 'Enable Expert mode, then Menu → Developer → Custom networks: enter the name, Chain ID, symbol and the RPC URL (https).',
